WEBVTT

00:02.550 --> 00:03.968
KATARA: Water...

00:04.844 --> 00:06.012
Earth...

00:06.846 --> 00:08.139
Fire...

00:08.890 --> 00:10.183
Air.

00:11.017 --> 00:14.771
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.438 --> 00:18.525
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.484 --> 00:22.153
Only the Avatar,
master of all 4 elements,

00:22.278 --> 00:23.446
could stop them.

00:23.571 --> 00:25.573
But when the world
needed him most,

00:25.698 --> 00:26.824
he vanished.

00:27.242 --> 00:28.326
100 years passed,

00:28.409 --> 00:30.912
And my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar―

00:30.995 --> 00:32.539
An airbender named Aang.

00:32.914 --> 00:35.041
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:35.124 --> 00:37.710
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.794 --> 00:38.795
AANG: Oof!

00:38.878 --> 00:41.673
KATARA: But I believe Aang
can save the world.

00:56.399 --> 00:58.568
SOKKA: You guys
are gonna be done soon, right?

00:58.652 --> 01:02.113
We've got a lot of ground to cover
If we want to make it to Omashu today.

01:02.197 --> 01:04.908
What, like you're ready
to go right now, naked guy?

01:05.033 --> 01:06.743
I could be ready in two minutes.

01:06.826 --> 01:08.245
Seriously. Whenever.

01:08.370 --> 01:11.081
So, you were showing me
the octopus form.

01:11.206 --> 01:12.958
Right. Let me see your stance.

01:16.836 --> 01:18.213
Your arms are too far apart.

01:18.296 --> 01:21.258
See, if you move them
closer together, you protect your center.

01:21.341 --> 01:23.426
- You got it?
- Oh. Yeah.

01:23.510 --> 01:24.511
Thanks.

01:26.054 --> 01:27.430
Ok, let's see what you got.

01:45.448 --> 01:48.326
You make a fine octopus, pupil Aang.

01:50.620 --> 01:51.955
( SPLASH )

01:52.080 --> 01:54.207
( MUSIC PLAYING )

01:54.666 --> 01:56.751
( MAN HUMMING )

01:56.918 --> 01:58.003
♪ Don't fall in love

01:58.086 --> 02:00.130
♪ With a traveling girl

02:00.255 --> 02:01.881
♪ She'll leave you broke

02:01.965 --> 02:04.134
♪ And broken-hearted

02:04.217 --> 02:05.802
( MUSIC STOPS )

02:05.927 --> 02:07.512
Hey, hey! River people.

02:08.054 --> 02:09.222
We're not river people.

02:09.764 --> 02:10.849
You're not?

02:10.932 --> 02:12.892
Well, then what kind
of people are you?

02:12.976 --> 02:14.477
Just people.

02:14.853 --> 02:17.147
Aren't we all, brother? Hoo!

02:17.230 --> 02:18.398
Who are you?

02:18.481 --> 02:19.482
I'm Chong.

02:19.566 --> 02:20.942
And this is my wife, Lily.

02:21.026 --> 02:22.110
We're nomads.

02:22.193 --> 02:24.612
Happy to go wherever
the wind takes us.

02:24.696 --> 02:25.780
( SINGS GIBBERISH )

02:26.239 --> 02:27.490
You guys are nomads?!

02:27.574 --> 02:29.617
That's great! I'm a nomad!

02:29.993 --> 02:31.494
Hey! Me, too!

02:31.911 --> 02:33.079
I know.

02:33.163 --> 02:34.247
You just said that.

02:34.331 --> 02:37.417
Oh. Nice underwear.

02:40.170 --> 02:42.088
( GASPS )

02:43.631 --> 02:44.716
( GRUNTING )

02:44.799 --> 02:46.468
I didn't find anything to eat.

02:46.551 --> 02:48.136
I can't live like this.

02:48.219 --> 02:49.971
I wasn't meant to be a fugitive.

02:50.055 --> 02:51.639
This is impossible!

02:52.182 --> 02:53.183
Uncle...

02:53.266 --> 02:54.642
What are you doing?

02:55.310 --> 02:57.979
You're looking at
the rare white dragon bush.

02:58.104 --> 03:03.193
Its leaves make a tea
so delicious it's heartbreaking.

03:03.318 --> 03:06.363
That, or it's the white jade bush,

03:06.446 --> 03:08.031
which is poisonous.

03:08.531 --> 03:10.283
We need food, not tea.

03:10.367 --> 03:12.035
I'm going fishing.

03:12.118 --> 03:14.496
Hmm. Delectable tea,

03:14.579 --> 03:16.373
or deadly poison?

03:18.333 --> 03:20.335
( LOWING )

03:21.711 --> 03:24.506
AANG: Hey, Sokka,
You should hear some of these stories.

03:24.756 --> 03:26.549
These guys have
been everywhere.

03:26.633 --> 03:29.094
Well, not everywhere,
little arrowhead,

03:29.177 --> 03:30.762
but where we haven't been,

03:30.845 --> 03:33.390
we've heard about
through stories and songs.

03:34.307 --> 03:36.976
They said they'll take us to see
a giant night crawler.

03:37.060 --> 03:41.773
MOKU: On the way, there's a waterfall
that creates a never-ending rainbow!

03:41.898 --> 03:43.775
Look, I hate to be
the wet blanket here,

03:43.858 --> 03:46.319
but since Katara is busy,
I guess it's up to me.

03:46.694 --> 03:48.196
We need to get to Omashu.

03:48.321 --> 03:52.033
No sidetracks, no worms,
and definitely no rainbows.

03:52.909 --> 03:57.330
Whoa! Sounds like someone's
got a case of destination fever.

03:57.414 --> 03:58.456
( LAUGHS )

03:58.540 --> 04:00.834
You're worried too much about
where you're going.

04:01.126 --> 04:03.294
LILY: You gotta focus
less on the where

04:03.378 --> 04:04.879
and more on the going.

04:05.380 --> 04:06.423
Oh...

04:06.506 --> 04:07.590
Ma...

04:07.674 --> 04:08.675
Shu!

04:09.092 --> 04:10.093
Sokka's right.

04:10.176 --> 04:13.680
We need to find King Bumi so Aang
can learn earthbending somewhere safe.

04:13.763 --> 04:15.723
Well, sounds like you're
headed to Omashu.

04:16.933 --> 04:19.436
There's an old story
about a secret pass...

04:19.978 --> 04:22.814
Right through the mountains.

04:23.565 --> 04:25.400
Is this real or a legend?

04:25.483 --> 04:27.235
Oh, it's a real legend.

04:27.318 --> 04:30.113
And it's as old as earthbending itself.

04:30.488 --> 04:32.031
( STRUMMING )

04:32.115 --> 04:33.158
( HUMMING )

04:33.241 --> 04:34.868
♪ Two lovers

04:34.951 --> 04:37.412
♪ Forbidden from one another

04:37.495 --> 04:42.333
♪ A war divides their people

04:42.417 --> 04:46.588
♪ And a mountain divides them apart

04:48.214 --> 04:53.636
♪ Built a path to be together ♪

04:53.720 --> 04:55.763
Yeah, I forget the next couple lines,

04:55.847 --> 04:57.265
but then it goes...

04:57.348 --> 04:59.517
♪ Secret tunnel

04:59.601 --> 05:02.437
♪ Secret tunnel

05:02.562 --> 05:04.731
♪ Through the mountain

05:04.814 --> 05:09.068
♪ Secret, secret, secret, secret tunnel

05:09.152 --> 05:10.153
♪ Yeah ♪

05:10.236 --> 05:11.654
( APPLAUSE )

05:11.738 --> 05:13.698
I think we'll just
stick with flying.

05:13.781 --> 05:16.117
We've dealt with the Fire Nation before.

05:16.201 --> 05:17.285
We'll be fine.

05:17.368 --> 05:20.413
Yeah, thanks for the help,
but Appa hates going underground.

05:20.497 --> 05:23.082
And we need to do
whatever makes Appa most comfortable.

05:23.166 --> 05:24.167
( LOWING )

05:24.250 --> 05:25.251
Launch!

05:25.335 --> 05:27.253
( SNARLING )

05:29.255 --> 05:31.007
( SCREAMING )

05:31.966 --> 05:34.010
Secret love cave. Let's go.

05:42.644 --> 05:46.105
IROH: Zuko, remember that plant
I thought might be tea?

05:46.564 --> 05:47.899
You didn't.

05:47.982 --> 05:49.275
I did.

05:49.359 --> 05:50.777
And it wasn't.

05:50.860 --> 05:51.986
Aagh!

05:52.320 --> 05:54.322
When the rash spreads
to my throat,

05:54.405 --> 05:56.074
I will stop breathing.

05:56.157 --> 05:57.700
But look what I found!

05:58.117 --> 05:59.786
These are pakui berries.

05:59.869 --> 06:03.164
Known to cure the poison
of the white jade plant!

06:03.748 --> 06:07.502
That, or makaola berries,
that cause blindness.

06:07.877 --> 06:10.463
We're not taking any more chances
with these plants!

06:10.547 --> 06:12.048
We need to get help.

06:12.131 --> 06:13.925
But where are we going to go?

06:14.467 --> 06:16.719
We're enemies of the Earth Kingdom,

06:16.803 --> 06:19.556
and fugitives from the Fire Nation.

06:20.890 --> 06:22.517
If the Earth Kingdom discovers us,

06:22.642 --> 06:24.269
they'll have us killed.

06:24.352 --> 06:26.604
But if the Fire Nation discovers us,

06:26.688 --> 06:28.690
We'll be turned over to Azula.

06:30.275 --> 06:31.901
Earth kingdom it is.

06:32.819 --> 06:34.779
SOKKA: How far are we
from the tunnel?

06:34.862 --> 06:36.864
Actually, it's not just one tunnel.

06:36.948 --> 06:40.243
The lovers didn't want anyone
to find out about their love,

06:40.326 --> 06:42.453
so they built a whole labyrinth.

06:43.204 --> 06:44.664
Labyrinth?!

06:44.747 --> 06:46.249
I'm sure we'll figure it out.

06:48.251 --> 06:51.087
All you need to
do is trust in love,

06:51.170 --> 06:53.131
according to the curse.

06:56.634 --> 06:57.635
( GROWLS )

06:57.719 --> 06:58.761
Curse?!

07:00.263 --> 07:02.098
CHONG: Hey, hey! We're here!

07:02.515 --> 07:04.517
SOKKA: What exactly is this curse?

07:05.143 --> 07:07.812
The curse says that only
those that trust in love

07:07.895 --> 07:09.689
can make it through the caves.

07:09.772 --> 07:11.899
Otherwise, you'll be
trapped in them forever.

07:11.983 --> 07:13.026
And die.

07:13.651 --> 07:15.194
Oh, yeah, and die.

07:15.903 --> 07:16.946
Hey!

07:17.030 --> 07:18.906
I just remembered
the rest of that song.

07:19.365 --> 07:22.243
( STRUMS ) ♪ And die ♪

07:22.660 --> 07:26.164
That's it! There's no way
we're going through some cursed hole!

07:27.332 --> 07:30.877
Hey! Someone's making a big campfire!

07:31.294 --> 07:33.338
That's no campfire, Moku.

07:33.421 --> 07:34.547
It's Fire Nation.

07:34.631 --> 07:35.923
They're tracking us.

07:36.674 --> 07:39.677
So, all you need is to trust in love
to get through these caves?

07:39.761 --> 07:42.138
That is correct,
Master Arrowhead.

07:48.144 --> 07:49.312
We can make it.

07:49.395 --> 07:50.772
Everyone into the hole.

07:53.191 --> 07:55.068
( SNARLS )

08:01.574 --> 08:02.575
SOLDIER: Hold on!

08:02.659 --> 08:03.701
It's too dangerous.

08:04.035 --> 08:05.953
Haven't you heard the song?

08:06.037 --> 08:07.622
Just close them in.

08:07.705 --> 08:09.916
The mountain will take care of the rest.

08:25.765 --> 08:27.684
( GROWLING )

08:28.309 --> 08:30.436
KATARA: It's ok, Appa. We'll be fine.

08:30.520 --> 08:31.688
I hope.

08:31.979 --> 08:33.523
We will be fine.

08:33.606 --> 08:34.857
All we need
is a plan.

08:34.941 --> 08:36.776
Chong, how long do those torches last?

08:36.859 --> 08:38.528
Um, about two hours each.

08:39.278 --> 08:42.365
And we have five torches,
so that's 10 hours.

08:42.448 --> 08:45.785
It doesn't work like that
if they're all lit at the same time!

08:45.868 --> 08:47.578
Oh! Right.

08:47.662 --> 08:50.957
I'm gonna make a map
to keep track of exactly where we've been.

08:51.040 --> 08:54.836
Then we should be able to
solve it like a maze and get through.

08:56.963 --> 08:58.840
( APPA GROWLS )

09:03.845 --> 09:06.180
WOMAN: You two must not
be from around here.

09:06.264 --> 09:08.683
We know better
than to touch the white jade.

09:08.766 --> 09:11.436
Much less make it into tea and drink it.

09:12.019 --> 09:13.229
( LAUGHS ) Oops!

09:14.147 --> 09:17.066
- So, where are you traveling from?
- Yes, we're travelers.

09:17.442 --> 09:18.943
Do you have names?

09:19.026 --> 09:20.361
Names?

09:20.445 --> 09:22.029
Of course we have names.

09:22.613 --> 09:24.323
I'm... Lee.

09:24.407 --> 09:26.117
And this is my uncle...

09:26.200 --> 09:27.869
Uh, Mushi.

09:29.245 --> 09:31.539
Yes, my nephew was named
after his father,

09:31.622 --> 09:34.083
so just call him Junior.

09:34.542 --> 09:36.252
Mushi and Junior, huh?

09:36.335 --> 09:37.628
My name is Song.

09:38.212 --> 09:40.506
You two look like you
could use a good meal.

09:40.590 --> 09:42.049
Why don't you stay for dinner?

09:42.425 --> 09:44.761
Sorry, but we need to be moving on.

09:44.844 --> 09:45.845
That's too bad.

09:45.928 --> 09:48.055
My mom always makes
too much roast duck.

09:48.139 --> 09:49.724
Where do you live exactly?!

09:52.268 --> 09:55.188
Sokka, this is the tenth dead end
you've led us to.

09:55.438 --> 09:58.566
This doesn't make any sense.
We already came through this way.

09:58.649 --> 10:00.485
CHONG: We don't need a map.

10:00.568 --> 10:02.111
We just need love.

10:02.653 --> 10:03.988
The little guy knows it.

10:04.071 --> 10:06.449
Yeah, but I wouldn't mind a map, also.

10:06.949 --> 10:09.410
SOKKA: There's something strange here.

10:09.494 --> 10:11.329
There's only one explanation.

10:12.413 --> 10:13.706
The tunnels are changing.

10:14.081 --> 10:15.750
( RUMBLING )

10:15.833 --> 10:17.627
( CHITTERING )

10:20.671 --> 10:22.465
My daughter tells me you're refugees.

10:22.799 --> 10:25.218
We were once refugees ourselves.

10:25.468 --> 10:29.764
When I was a little girl, the Fire Nation
raided our farming village.

10:29.847 --> 10:32.308
All the men were taken away.

10:32.391 --> 10:34.435
That was the last time I saw my father.

10:36.145 --> 10:38.773
I haven't seen my father
in many years.

10:39.482 --> 10:41.943
Oh. Is he fighting in the war?

10:45.655 --> 10:46.656
Yeah.

10:52.119 --> 10:53.454
CHONG: The tunnels...

10:53.538 --> 10:54.705
They're a-changing.

10:54.789 --> 10:56.415
It must be the curse.

10:56.499 --> 10:59.377
I knew we shouldn't
have come down here.

10:59.460 --> 11:02.255
Right. If only we'd listened to you.

11:02.338 --> 11:04.799
KATARA: Everyone be quiet. Listen!

11:05.716 --> 11:07.385
( WAILING )

11:14.058 --> 11:15.518
( SNARLING )

11:17.687 --> 11:19.689
A giant flying thing with teeth!

11:21.315 --> 11:22.984
No! It's a wolf-bat!

11:31.367 --> 11:33.286
( ROARS )

11:48.885 --> 11:50.136
( GRUNTING )

11:50.887 --> 11:52.013
( SCREAMING )

12:02.064 --> 12:03.983
( GROWLING )

12:07.194 --> 12:09.071
( PANTING )

12:09.155 --> 12:11.407
( SCREAMING )

12:11.490 --> 12:12.742
Yeah, it's no use.

12:12.825 --> 12:13.993
We're separated.

12:14.243 --> 12:16.078
But at least you have us.

12:16.162 --> 12:17.204
( LAUGHS )

12:17.330 --> 12:19.999
( SCREAMS )

12:29.967 --> 12:31.385
Can I join you?

12:31.469 --> 12:33.054
I know what you've been through.

12:33.137 --> 12:35.097
We've all been through it.

12:35.932 --> 12:37.934
The Fire Nation has hurt you.

12:44.482 --> 12:45.942
It's ok.

12:46.025 --> 12:47.568
They've hurt me, too.

12:53.532 --> 12:56.827
( UPBEAT STRUMMING )

12:56.911 --> 12:59.747
♪ Oh, don't let the cave-in
get you down

13:01.082 --> 13:03.167
♪ Don't let the falling rocks

13:03.250 --> 13:05.962
♪ Turn your smile into a frown

13:06.420 --> 13:09.006
♪ When the tunnel's at its darkest

13:09.090 --> 13:10.841
♪ That's when you need a clown

13:10.925 --> 13:12.093
♪ Hey

13:12.927 --> 13:17.223
♪ Don't let the cave-in
get you down, Sokka ♪

13:23.729 --> 13:25.106
Aang, look!

13:25.898 --> 13:27.358
AANG: We found the exit!

13:28.359 --> 13:30.069
( STRAINING )

13:30.152 --> 13:32.571
( APPA GROWLS )

13:36.993 --> 13:38.327
( SCREAMING )

13:49.463 --> 13:51.048
This isn't the exit.

13:51.132 --> 13:52.299
No.

13:52.800 --> 13:53.968
It's a tomb.

14:10.484 --> 14:12.862
AANG: It must be the two
lovers from the legend.

14:12.987 --> 14:14.363
That's who is buried here.

14:15.823 --> 14:17.867
These pictures tell their story.

14:27.043 --> 14:30.463
KATARA: They met on top of the mountain
that divided their two villages.

14:32.131 --> 14:35.509
The villages were enemies,
so they could not be together.

14:36.343 --> 14:39.055
But their love was strong,
and they found a way.

14:42.725 --> 14:45.478
The two lovers learned earthbending
from the badger-moles.

14:45.561 --> 14:48.064
They became the first earthbenders.

14:48.147 --> 14:51.192
They built elaborate tunnels
so that they could meet secretly.

14:52.610 --> 14:54.111
Anyone who tried to follow them

14:54.195 --> 14:56.072
would be lost forever in the labyrinth.

14:58.657 --> 15:00.743
But one day, the man didn't come.

15:02.828 --> 15:05.289
He died in the war between
their two villages.

15:08.167 --> 15:10.503
Devastated, the woman
unleashed a terrible display

15:10.586 --> 15:12.671
of her earthbending power.

15:12.755 --> 15:14.757
She could have destroyed them all...

15:16.383 --> 15:19.261
But instead she declared the war over.

15:19.345 --> 15:23.224
Both villages helped her build a new city
where they would live together in peace.

15:25.142 --> 15:28.687
The woman's name was Oma,
and the man's name was Shu.

15:29.688 --> 15:31.607
The great city was named Omashu

15:31.690 --> 15:33.692
as a monument to their love.

15:39.740 --> 15:42.910
"Love is brightest
in the dark."

15:46.580 --> 15:47.998
MOKU: Oh, great!

15:48.082 --> 15:50.334
Your plans have led us
to another dead end.

15:50.793 --> 15:52.711
SOKKA: At least I'm thinking of ideas

15:52.795 --> 15:55.631
and trying to get is out of here, Moku.

15:56.048 --> 15:57.341
Whoa, whoa. Wait a minute.

15:57.424 --> 15:58.717
We're thinking of ideas?

15:58.801 --> 16:01.470
'Cause I've had an idea
for, like, an hour now.

16:01.554 --> 16:02.805
Yes!

16:02.888 --> 16:05.599
We're all thinking of ideas!

16:05.933 --> 16:07.476
Well, then listen to this.

16:07.560 --> 16:09.395
If love is the key out of here,

16:09.478 --> 16:12.481
then all we need to do
is play a love song.

16:13.065 --> 16:15.109
( STRUMMING )

16:17.111 --> 16:19.780
AANG: How are we gonna
find our way out of these tunnels?

16:19.864 --> 16:21.615
I have a crazy idea.

16:21.699 --> 16:22.700
What?

16:23.159 --> 16:25.619
Never mind. It's too crazy.

16:25.703 --> 16:27.079
Katara, what is it?

16:27.163 --> 16:28.455
I was thinking...

16:28.914 --> 16:31.125
The curse says we'll be
trapped in here forever

16:31.208 --> 16:32.585
unless we trust in love.

16:32.668 --> 16:33.961
Right.

16:34.044 --> 16:37.256
And here it says
"love is brightest in the dark"

16:37.339 --> 16:39.675
And has a picture of them kissing.

16:40.009 --> 16:41.468
Where are you going with this?

16:41.802 --> 16:43.387
Well...

16:43.470 --> 16:44.889
What if we kissed?

16:44.972 --> 16:46.599
Us, kissing?

16:46.682 --> 16:49.101
See? It was a crazy idea.

16:49.185 --> 16:50.519
Us...

16:51.270 --> 16:52.271
Kissing.

16:52.354 --> 16:53.355
( SCOFFS )

16:53.439 --> 16:55.983
Us, kissing.
What was I thinking?!

16:56.066 --> 16:57.693
Can you imagine that?

16:57.776 --> 16:59.570
Yeah. ( LAUGHS AWKWARDLY )

16:59.653 --> 17:01.697
I definitely wouldn't want to kiss you.

17:02.740 --> 17:05.743
Oh. Well, I didn't realize
it was such a horrible option.

17:06.452 --> 17:07.912
Sorry I suggested it.

17:07.995 --> 17:09.413
No, no. I mean...

17:09.496 --> 17:12.249
If it was a choice between kissing you
and dying...

17:12.333 --> 17:14.126
- Oh!
- What?!

17:14.210 --> 17:17.755
I'm saying I would rather
kiss you than die. That's a compliment.

17:17.838 --> 17:20.257
Well, I'm not sure
which I would rather do.

17:21.383 --> 17:22.927
What is wrong with me?

17:24.678 --> 17:28.182
( STRUMMING TUNE )

17:30.267 --> 17:32.144
♪ Even if you're lost

17:32.228 --> 17:34.355
♪ You can't lose the love

17:34.438 --> 17:37.358
♪ Because it's in your heart

17:38.025 --> 17:41.195
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

17:43.405 --> 17:44.907
IROH: Thank you for the duck.

17:44.990 --> 17:46.700
It was excellent.

17:46.784 --> 17:47.868
You're welcome.

17:47.952 --> 17:52.039
It brings me joy to see someone
eat my cooking with such gusto.

17:52.456 --> 17:54.083
Much practice.

17:56.085 --> 17:58.128
Junior, where are your manners?

17:58.254 --> 18:01.173
You need to thank these nice people.

18:01.840 --> 18:03.050
Thank you.

18:03.133 --> 18:06.262
SONG: I know you don't think
there's any hope left in the world,

18:06.345 --> 18:07.638
but there is hope.

18:07.721 --> 18:09.306
The Avatar has returned.

18:10.599 --> 18:11.892
I know.

18:16.772 --> 18:18.399
( LOWING )

18:25.531 --> 18:27.032
What are you doing?!

18:27.116 --> 18:30.369
These people just
showed you great kindness.

18:30.452 --> 18:32.746
They're about to show us
a little more kindness.

18:33.539 --> 18:34.540
Well?

18:50.264 --> 18:53.142
AANG: We're gonna run out of light
any second now, aren't we?

18:53.559 --> 18:55.019
I think so.

18:55.102 --> 18:56.395
Then, what are we gonna do?

18:57.688 --> 18:58.897
What can we do?

19:22.796 --> 19:24.923
( STRUMMING )

19:25.007 --> 19:26.592
( GROWLING )

19:33.432 --> 19:34.850
( SNARLING )

19:38.312 --> 19:39.730
( SCREAMING )

19:43.901 --> 19:46.028
CHONG: Hey! You saved us, Sokka!

19:46.779 --> 19:49.448
No. They were trying
to get away from something.

19:49.823 --> 19:50.824
From what?

19:50.908 --> 19:51.909
( RUMBLING )

19:56.205 --> 19:57.790
( GROWLING )

20:15.682 --> 20:16.725
Aagh!

20:16.809 --> 20:17.935
Oof!

20:21.855 --> 20:23.774
( CHORD STRUMS )

20:29.071 --> 20:33.075
( CONTINUES STRUMMING )

20:33.158 --> 20:35.786
Hey, those things are music-lovers!

20:36.078 --> 20:39.164
♪ Badger-moles coming towards me

20:39.248 --> 20:40.290
♪ Come on, guys

20:40.374 --> 20:41.625
♪ Help me out

20:42.584 --> 20:44.795
♪ The big bad badger-moles

20:44.878 --> 20:46.046
♪ Who opened the tunnels

20:46.130 --> 20:47.256
♪ Hate the wolf-bats

20:47.339 --> 20:49.716
♪ But love the sounds ♪

20:51.051 --> 20:53.512
AANG: It's made of some kind of crystals.

20:53.595 --> 20:55.347
They must only light up in the dark.

20:55.431 --> 20:57.433
That's how the two lovers
found each other.

20:57.516 --> 21:00.310
They just put out their lights
and followed the crystals.

21:02.771 --> 21:04.022
That must be the way out!

21:07.693 --> 21:09.069
So, um...

21:09.153 --> 21:10.154
Let's go!

21:15.701 --> 21:16.785
( GROWLS )

21:29.715 --> 21:30.799
What about Sokka?!

21:31.425 --> 21:33.427
( RUMBLING )

21:35.012 --> 21:36.221
( SNARLING )

21:38.807 --> 21:39.808
Sokka!

21:41.935 --> 21:43.395
How did you guys get out?!

21:43.479 --> 21:45.022
Just like the legend says―

21:45.105 --> 21:46.523
We let love lead the way.

21:46.607 --> 21:49.985
Really? We let huge ferocious beasts
lead our way.

21:51.862 --> 21:54.364
( GROWLING )

21:57.951 --> 21:59.578
( CHITTERING )

22:01.330 --> 22:03.081
( ROARS )

22:06.210 --> 22:07.753
Why is your forehead all red?

22:08.837 --> 22:11.840
Nobody react
to what I'm about to tell you.

22:12.216 --> 22:13.634
I think that kid

22:13.717 --> 22:15.427
might be the Avatar.

22:19.556 --> 22:22.017
AANG: So, are you guys
gonna come to Omashu with us?

22:22.142 --> 22:23.685
- Nope.
- Ok.

22:23.769 --> 22:25.103
Thanks for everything, Moku.

22:27.105 --> 22:28.232
Sokka,

22:28.315 --> 22:31.860
I hope you learned a little something
about not letting the plans

22:31.944 --> 22:33.654
get in the way of the journey.

22:35.739 --> 22:37.241
Just play your songs.

22:37.866 --> 22:39.451
Hey! Good plan!

22:39.576 --> 22:41.662
( STRUMMING )

22:43.497 --> 22:45.249
♪ Even if you're lost

22:45.415 --> 22:47.501
♪ You can't lose the love

22:47.626 --> 22:51.255
♪ Because it's in your heart

22:51.380 --> 22:55.300
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

22:56.760 --> 22:58.929
SOKKA: The journey
was long and annoying,

22:59.012 --> 23:01.306
but now you get to see
what it's really about―

23:01.390 --> 23:02.933
The destination.

23:03.141 --> 23:04.393
I present to you

23:04.476 --> 23:06.979
the Earth Kingdom city of O―

23:08.146 --> 23:09.731
Oh, no!

23:21.326 --> 23:23.328
( MEN CHANTING RHYTHMICALLY )
